// Kaleidoscope Cookery in a real client: water keeps its grade through the stockpot and the teapot,
// sea water goes through the stockpot and the teapot and comes back out salty, a teapot of sea water
// brews nothing while one of fresh water brews, a teapot picked up and placed again keeps its water's
// grade, a teapot item scooping world water samples it, sea water included,
// and dripstone fills a teapot with dripstonePurity water. It runs on every node with the
// integration, 1.21.1-neoforge and the five Fabric ones. Only the 1.21.1 builds let dripstone fill a
// teapot, so on the others dripGraded and pureF fail, and are the only lines that may. On 1.21.11,
// Refabricated 1.3.0.x has no tea bags and brews barley tea from twelve wheat seeds, and a teapot
// with no recipe for its ingredient throws it out, so freshBrews and seaKeepsBag fail there too. To
// check the teapot there, run a copy with every kaleidoscope_cookery:barley_tea_bag replaced by
// minecraft:wheat_seeds and the two count:1 beside it by count:12. Run it unattended in a singleplayer
// world:
//     ./gradlew ":<node>:runClient" -Pagent=tools/agent/integrations/kaleidoscope-cookery.jsonl -Pquickplay=KaleidoscopeAgent
// KaleidoscopeAgent is a throwaway world, made fresh for each run by
//     python tools/agent/new_world.py <node> KaleidoscopeAgent
// Then check what it recorded:
//     python tools/agent/drive.py run/<node>/agent/client tools/agent/integrations/kaleidoscope-cookery.jsonl --verify --max-age 15
// Every "execute" line checks that it said "Test passed", and the captures in
// run/<node>/agent/client/screenshots/ show Jade's line under a stockpot and a teapot.
//
// The blocks are right clicked by standing on them and looking straight down, as in
// supplementaries.jsonl. The player is addressed by selector: a NeoForge dev client names its player Dev, a Fabric one Player<NN>.
//
// A grade is stored on the block as one int, thirstwastaken2:water_quality: 1 to 4 for Dirty, Murky,
// Clean and Pure, 5 for sea water, as a cauldron stores it.

{"id": "load", "command": "wait", "args": {"ticks": 400}}
{"id": "arrived", "command": "client.state"}
{"id": "survival", "command": "server.command", "args": {"command": "gamemode survival @p"}}
