// An empty teapot in the hand scoops water out of the world as a bucket does, and the water is
// sampled where it lay: a swamp pool gives Dirty water, an ocean pool sea water. Each pool is a strip
// of source blocks in the floor, looked at from the dry floor to its north.
// Biomes are set four blocks at a time, and reading one blends in the cells next to it, differently
// on every seed, so each pool's biome covers every cell around its own and a cell of neither lies
// between the two.
{"id": "swampBiome", "command": "server.command", "args": {"command": "fillbiome -8 192 -8 3 207 7 minecraft:swamp"}}
{"id": "swampPool", "command": "server.command", "args": {"command": "fill -3 199 -1 -3 199 1 minecraft:water"}}
